# 50-prefix re-baseline — THRESHOLD LEG, raised thresholds (BACKLOG §25 item 5)
# Load-aware factor 3.0 / floor 4 (the raised thresholds D2 validated at 50 prefixes,
# P99 -6%). This leg decides whether 3.0/4 should replace the shipped 2.0/2 default.
# Run into its OWN output dir:
#   ./scripts/bench-runner.sh --suite custom \
#       --file docs/benchmarks/rebaseline/threshold-3.0-4.runs \
#       --repeat 3 --output-dir benchmark-reports/rebaseline/thr_3.0_4
# !!! 2026-09-30 audit: --load-imbalance-factor/--floor are INERT under the shipped
# bounded_load hash strategy (router_service.cpp compute_load_allowance); bench.sh now
# REFUSES this combination. The line below adds --hash-strategy jump so the flags govern
# the allowance — which means this leg answers the factor/floor question UNDER JUMP, not
# under the shipped strategy. The live leg for the shipped strategy is the epsilon leg:
#   ./scripts/bench-runner.sh --suite epsilon
--compare --model meta-llama/CodeLlama-13b-Instruct-hf --warmup --duration 30m --users 30 --max-model-len 8192 --prefix-ratio 0.9 --prompt-dist stress --hash-strategy jump --load-imbalance-factor 3.0 --load-imbalance-floor 4
